  "id": "normality",
  "term": "normality",
  "definition": "Normality refers to the socially expected range of behavior against which people are judged in families, schools, and other institutions. In this context, it is not a fixed trait but a shifting standard shaped by medical and social ideas about what counts as ordinary or deviant.",
